+# Judiciary evidence addendum — cycle `e645314aa32271f66d46b955279379d9`
+
+This dated addendum supplements the four filed case outcomes and the original cycle report. It is new evidence, not a new random sample or a retroactive change to the frozen batch.
+
+## AssemblyP1 #249 — delivery and deployment independently confirmed
+
+The earlier cycle report verified source landing but lacked deployment evidence. Fresh independent GitHub API reads now establish:
+
+- Public remote `main` is `65aa5f0ba73684a19bac86b2249d6101ab96aa4c`; the sampled delivery head `3b3b064c7753a3adc1c57f67cf62ee6873a92044` is an ancestor of that main head.
+- GitHub Actions runs for the exact current main head include **CI**, **Documents**, **Slides and Pages**, and **Signed commits**, all completed successfully on 2026-11-03 (`https://github.com/ottojung/assemblyp1/actions/runs/41736839099`, `/41736838741`, `/41736838705`, `/41736838668`). These are GitHub-hosted checks, not Viche agent execution.
+- GitHub Pages deployment `7533089883` deployed the same main SHA to `https://ottojung.github.io/assemblyp1/`; deployment status is `success` (2026-11-03T23:10:02Z). Independent GETs of the portal and both configured deck paths returned successful HTTP responses.
+
+This strengthens the existing `verified` outcome from source delivery only to verified merge, successful hosted CI and Pages deployment. It verifies the infrastructure deliverable's intended outcome at that deployed SHA. It does not establish current continuing uptime beyond the observed reads, nor quality/completion of separately assigned deck-content issues #250/#251.
+
+## Executive Innovation Office Act — live integrity failure persists
+
+The current ordinary law text `government/LAWS.md` §§236–248 describes Act 24 as enacted with an imprecise `2026-10-31T06:XXZ` time and cites its vote. The sampled commit `c3534c7bdff8b8c071dd4e8d0fb67d94c31ac4d1` remains a draft-only edit; later merge `8edf196782fba586c2b2ac4d975a1fd47abb5b39` contains the Act/law change. A fresh `sh government/tally.sh executive-innovation-office-act` still exits 2 with `Invalid, duplicate or mismatched ballot` after `predict-gate: PASS (not_exercised)`. The tally failure is direct evidence that current protected ballot integrity cannot be reproduced by the present checker; it is not, by itself, proof that the historical vote did not occur or that the sampled draft-only commit enacted the Act. The case therefore remains `inconclusive` as previously filed. Canonical checkout was read only and is dirty; no record or ballot was changed.
+
+## Sample and measurement limits
+
+The saved random snapshot SHA256 remains `0010095cd556a089273266d7fff71713fd2764994e114340dea280aed4803bc6`; this addendum does not change sample composition or replace any verdict. The two ignored-work cases remain different: SoringP1 research is not an assigned deliverable on the verified evidence, while Ivanka has repeated scheduler activity on the issue's marceline-dev execution scope; this is a host/execution finding, not a claim that technical delivery was tested. No authenticated Ivanka current-main artifact was obtained. Four sampled cases cannot yield a precise population estimate. Missing technical evidence remains uncertainty, not a clean result or a misconduct finding.
