+# Judiciary bounded audit — cycle `e645314aa32271f66d46b955279379d9`
+
+**Scope.** Four frozen cases from `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/random/latest.json`, snapshot SHA256 `0010095cd556a089273266d7fff71713fd2764994e114340dea280aed4803bc6` (captured at 1794039249). All four per-case outcomes were filed with `government/audit-accountability.py report`; this report supplements, and does not replace, those outcome records. No correction to an earlier cycle was filed.
+
+## Adjudications
+
+| Case | Verdict | Basis and limits |
+|---|---|---|
+| `bfd2b7dbcd19fd1850` — SoringP1 FO(TC) research | `not_assigned` | The live issue remains open, but the sampled ignored-work case does not establish a current billy-dev execution assignment. The latest verified board dispatch described a bounded Billy-managed follow-up; research completion/artifacts were not independently checked. No neglect finding is inferred from an open issue. |
+| `705f97f5d5cef3bbac` — Ivanka assembler | `finding` | The issue explicitly limits execution to `marceline-dev`, while current standing host authorization is Billy-only. Recent scheduler comments repeatedly dispatch Viche agents for this work. This is a host-authorization finding about Viche agent execution, not GitHub-hosted CI, and not an adjudication of technical delivery. Current repository/main and the alleged fix were not independently inspected. |
+| `f215bdba3d202cf470` — AssemblyP1 Slidev | `verified` (source delivery only) | Independent public Git fetch verified sampled branch `3b3b064c7753a3adc1c57f67cf62ee6873a92044`, main `65aa5f0ba73684a19bac86b2249d6101ab96aa4c`, and that the branch is an ancestor of main. Main contains the Slidev project, lockfile, decks, portal, scripts and configuration. The GitHub status API showed pending/zero statuses for the sampled branch head; no Actions run, deployment, or live URL was verified. Thus this verifies source landing, not full CI/deployment acceptance. |
+| `35cd002d074f7bc366` — Executive Innovation Office Act draft decision | `inconclusive` | Sampled commit `c3534c7bdff8b8c071dd4e8d0fb67d94c31ac4d1` is in canonical history and only edits the bill draft; it is not itself enactment. Later merge `8edf196782fba586c2b2ac4d975a1fd47abb5b39` records M-024 enactment and adds the law. But the present `sh government/tally.sh executive-innovation-office-act` fails with `Invalid, duplicate or mismatched ballot` (exit 2), so current ballot integrity cannot be validated by rerun. Historical recorded enactment and current integrity failure remain distinct evidence. The canonical checkout was read-only; it had 103 dirty status entries. |
+
+## Measurement and uncertainty
+
+This is a four-case randomized sample, not an estimate precise enough to generalize performance or Founder happiness across the board. Two open-work cases had asymmetric source access: SoringP1 artifact delivery was not fetched, and Ivanka's current repository/main was not checked. For AssemblyP1, a public Git ancestry check strengthened the delivery claim, but pending status and absent deployment evidence leave production behavior unmeasured. For the government decision, recorded enactment history does not cure the current tally-integrity failure, and a failed current rerun alone does not prove the historical vote invalid. The sample therefore distinguishes a specific host finding from unassigned work and distinguishes code landing from verified deployment.
+
+Judiciary operations successfully froze and identified this distinct four-case cycle, inspected live board state, fetched a sampled remote branch independently, and filed a verdict for every case. Limits include no independent authentication of the execution host beyond issue dispatch/host instructions, no live deployment check, and a dirty canonical checkout that prevented safe publication there. The watchdog's aggregate counts are signals, not a clean bill or a guilt verdict. No policy or measurement-system reform is proposed here; these findings and limitations are submitted for legislative consideration.
